{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "My recent trip to Japan was a truly unforgettable experience. From the moment I arrived, I was struck by the country's unique blend of traditional and modern culture. The bustling streets of Tokyo were a sensory overload, with neon lights, giant billboards, and the hum of traffic filling the air.\n\nDespite the initial chaos, I soon found myself drawn to the serene beauty of Japan's temples and gardens. A visit to the famous Fushimi Inari shrine in Kyoto was a highlight, with its thousands of vermilion torii gates forming a tunnel up the mountain. The peaceful atmosphere and stunning scenery made for a truly meditative experience.\n\nOf course, no trip to Japan would be complete without trying the local cuisine. I was blown away by the freshness and simplicity of the food, from delicate sushi to hearty bowls of ramen. And let's not forget the unique drinking culture, with izakayas (Japanese gastropubs) offering a lively and convivial atmosphere.\n\nOne of the most memorable moments of my trip was a traditional tea ceremony, where I was taught the ancient art of preparing matcha. The slow, deliberate movements and attention to detail were a fascinating glimpse into Japan's rich cultural heritage.\n\nAs I reflect on my time in Japan, I'm struck by the country's ability to balance tradition and innovation. From ancient temples to cutting-edge technology, Japan is a country that seamlessly blends old and new. I'm already planning my next trip back to this incredible country.", "logprobs": [{"token": "My", "logprob": -0.40969008207321167}, {"token": " recent", "logprob": -0.003243544837459922}, {"token": " trip", "logprob": -6.9141146923357155e-06}, {"token": " to", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -6.556489552167477e-06}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.20399616658687592}, {"t